From 1f4551aaf04d3030731695d650542a57c00330d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lucas Santos <lsantos7654@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 7 May 2026 23:28:59 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 23/26] Ephemeral subagent sessions
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds an `ephemeral` boolean to sessions. When set, the session is
deleted automatically when its runner reaches idle on a terminal
turn (completed | failed | cancelled). For background-mode
subagents the delete is deferred until the parent consumes the
buffered result via read_task_result, so the result isn't lost.

Subagents that aren't designed for resume — the memory daemon,
the expert curator, explore-style one-offs — accumulate in main's
session tree today. Manual cleanup via delete_session is the only
escape hatch. With this change the subagent tree only shows
long-lived agents (experts, team leads) plus any in-flight
one-offs; one-offs vanish when done.

Schema:

  - `session.ephemeral` boolean column with default false (Drizzle
    migration `20260508023927_session_ephemeral`)
  - `Session.Info` Zod schema field
  - `Session.toRow` / `fromRow` map it
  - `Session.create` / `Session.fork` accept `ephemeral?: boolean`

Finalizers:

  - `SessionRunState.onIdle` looks up the session and removes it
    when ephemeral and not registered as a background task
  - `SessionBackground.consume` removes the consumed session when
    ephemeral. New `SessionBackground.isRegistered(taskID)` helper
    discriminates background vs foreground at the run-state seam
  - Both finalizers use dynamic imports for the cross-module call
    to avoid a top-level cycle (background.ts already imports
    SessionRunState.assertNotBusy)

Task tool:

  - `Task(ephemeral?: boolean)` parameter, mutually exclusive with
    `task_id` (resume defeats ephemeral; rejected at the schema
    layer)
  - Effective ephemeral = per-spawn override OR agent frontmatter
    default. Agents that should always be ephemeral declare
    `ephemeral: true` in `agent.md` frontmatter
  - Pass-through to Session.create / Session.fork

Agent + config:

  - `Agent.Info.ephemeral` runtime field
  - Config Agent schema accepts `ephemeral` in frontmatter
  - Agent state composer threads it from cfg into the runtime info

Hivemind callsite:

  - `HivemindMemoryPlugin` auto-spawn passes `ephemeral: true` so
    the daemon's session vanishes after each compaction pass

Tests:

  - `test/session/ephemeral.test.ts` — round-trip, fork, consume()
    deletion semantics, isRegistered helper
  - `test/tool/task-ephemeral.test.ts` — per-spawn override,
    default false, mutual-exclusion with task_id, frontmatter
    default applied, per-spawn override beats frontmatter
  - `test/plugin/hivemind-memory.test.ts` extended to assert the
    auto-spawned daemon has ephemeral=true

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
